From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wowbox64: no x87 register conversion around unix calls

Every unix call of the x86 side (__wine_unix_call: each GL call of
WineD3D's command stream thread goes through one) saved the emulated FPU
into the WoW64 context and loaded it back, converting the eight x87
registers between double and 80-bit both ways. A unix call is a function
call for the x86 code, and the i386 ABI leaves the x87 and SSE registers
dead across it; only the control/status words and MXCSR live. Carry just
those for unix calls (the whole state when the call resets the context).
Syscalls are unchanged: they may get, set or raise on the context.

In a sea battle of Sid Meier's Pirates! the box64 runtime share of the
render thread went from 10% to 6%.

---
--- a/wine/wow64/wowbox64.c
+++ b/wine/wow64/wowbox64.c
@@ -452,7 +452,19 @@
         ctx->EFlags = emu->eflags.x64;
         cpu->Flags = 0;
 
-        box_to_fpu(ctx, emu);
+        /* A unix call is a function call for the x86 code: the x87 and SSE
+         * registers are dead across it by the i386 ABI, only the control
+         * and status words live. Converting the eight 80-bit registers both
+         * ways on every call (each GL call of WineD3D) is a few percent of
+         * a GL-heavy game's render thread. Syscalls (context get/set,
+         * exceptions) still carry the whole FPU state. */
+        if (is_unix_call) {
+            XMM_SAVE_AREA32* fpu = (XMM_SAVE_AREA32*)ctx->ExtendedRegisters;
+            fpu->MxCsr = emu->mxcsr.x32;
+            fpu->ControlWord = emu->cw.x16;
+            fpu->StatusWord = emu->sw.x16;
+        } else
+            box_to_fpu(ctx, emu);
 
         if (is_unix_call) {
             uintptr_t handle_low = Pop32(emu);
@@ -466,7 +478,13 @@
             R_EAX = Wow64SystemServiceEx(id, ULongToPtr(ctx->Esp + 4));
         }
 
-        fpu_to_box(ctx, emu);
+        if (is_unix_call && !(cpu->Flags & WOW64_CPURESERVED_FLAG_RESET_STATE)) {
+            XMM_SAVE_AREA32* fpu = (XMM_SAVE_AREA32*)ctx->ExtendedRegisters;
+            emu->mxcsr.x32 = fpu->MxCsr;
+            emu->cw.x16 = fpu->ControlWord;
+            emu->sw.x16 = fpu->StatusWord;
+        } else
+            fpu_to_box(ctx, emu);
 
         R_EBX = ctx->Ebx;
         R_ESI = ctx->Esi;
